This was apparently due, in part, to the athlete’s unfamiliarity with the starting instructions, which were given in Greek.  The final, however, was an absolutely fair start.  Archie Hahn defended the Olympic title he had won in St. Louis, winning fairly comfortably by about a yard.  The fight for second was very close, but " [:a {:href "/athletes/78817"} "Fay Moulton"] " edged ahead of " [:a {:href "/athletes/79575"} "Nigel  Barker"] " by inches near the line.  The other three finalists were not close."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "235"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78496"} "Archie Hahn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "12.0 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "11.4 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "11.2 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "414"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78817"} "Fay Moulton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "11.8 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "11.4 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "at 1 yard (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "44"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79575"} "Nigel Barker"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "– (2 h9)"] [:td {} "at 1 yard (2 h3)"] [:td {} "at 1 foot (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] 